  annotation "note_1771580141146_1", anchor: "ration-splitting, fire-tenders yielding warm shifts to the injured", text: "The ice-memory from this period is not tender. What it preserves is triage arithmetic — who eats, who doesn't, who freezes so that someone else might not. The sharing behaviors I describe here were real, but the entry's phrasing softens them into something resembling generosity. The tunnel survivors were not generous. They were desperate, and desperation produced a logic that happened to look like virtue. Gift-custom is built on that logic. It is stronger for it. Virtue would not have survived the first Long Dark.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
